1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
In this video, I will show you how to create a 3D model of Marvelous Designer.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,000
The Reversal function can help your model to get the ideal line and grid number.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
In Marvelous Designer, the model is a triangular face model.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,000
You can change the grid type and convert it into a four-sided face model with one click.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Select the version you want to edit, then right-click the grid type.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Here we choose to optimize the four sides.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Your model will be automatically converted into a four-sided model that is close to precision.

8
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Tips 1. The four-sided optimization function will move according to the shape of the panel and optimize the layout.

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Prevent the triangular face first.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
It is suitable for panels with a large body, sleeves, etc. and not so neat edges.

11
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
The four-sided grid function will place the panels according to the direction of the 2D interface.

12
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Tips 2. Prioritize the panel to generate a completely horizontal vertical line.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,000
At the edge of the slanted panel and the seam line, it will automatically connect and generate a triangular face.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
It is suitable for a regular rectangular panel that can be converted into a belt.

15
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Tips 3. Even if the panel is a regular rectangular panel, it must be placed in the 2D window to properly generate an horizontal vertical grid.

16
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Tips 4. You can also change the width of the panel.

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,000
You can use the optimization function of Everywhere to optimize the grid number of the model.

18
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Click Connect Everywhere.

19
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Enter your target grid number here.

20
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Then press the optimization button.

21
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:54,000
After the grid update is completed, you can observe that the number of grid numbers has decreased.

22
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Tips 2.

23
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:04,000
In the current version, the component material cannot be four-sided in the current version, but you can also adjust the grid number.

24
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Click the component column and select the component to be edited.

25
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Pull to the bottom and re-fill the number of faces you want.

26
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,000
You can see that the grid density has decreased.

27
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Or open the plane. The component model will be changed to exist in the form of a panel.

28
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Tips 3. You can also use the slope tool to customize the slope line of the clothing.

29
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Use the smart slope tool to create the slope model you need.

30
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Tips 4. The corresponding slope model will automatically be created on the mirror panel.

31
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Tips 5. You can connect multiple slope areas together.

32
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Tips 6. You can also use the slope tool to customize the slope line of the clothing.

33
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
You can also use the slope tool to customize the slope model you need.

34
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Finally, press the create button to create a slope.

35
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Tips 7. Use the edit slope tool to adjust the points that do not match the edge.

36
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Tips 8. The edge of the model will automatically generate black reference points according to the color relationship.

37
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Tips 9. You can also use the create slope tool to directly create a four-sided slope.

38
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Tips 10. In the create slope tool mode, press Ctrl and Shift and press a line.

39
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,000
You can also use the create slope tool to customize the slope model you need.

40
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
The points that do not fit the edge will also be added to the grid.

41
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:44,479
Tips 10. The new

42
00:03:44,479 --> 00:03:48,000
points will be added to the black reference points.

43
00:03:48,000 --> 00:04:03,759
In the 2D and 3D windows, you can configure and edit the

44
00:04:03,759 --> 00:04:07,079
model and your own.

45
00:04:07,079 --> 00:04:10,479
You can also change the size of the model.

46
00:04:10,479 --> 00:04:19,680
For example, if you want to change the size of the model, you can change the size of the model

47
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:22,899
by changing the size of the model.

48
00:04:22,899 --> 00:04:29,560
Or, you can change the size of the model by changing the size of the model.

49
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:32,579
This will determine whether you create a copy or replace the original grid by using the

50
00:04:32,579 --> 00:04:33,579
retouching grid.

51
00:04:33,579 --> 00:04:42,579
If you want to exit the network, please go to the file, exit, and select OBJ or FBX.

52
00:04:42,579 --> 00:04:48,579
In the exit window, you can find the option of merging near the peak.

53
00:04:48,579 --> 00:04:55,579
After opening the option, the peak within the range of the set merger will be merged.

54
00:04:55,579 --> 00:05:00,579
You can open the display option to check the welding situation of the border peak.

55
00:05:00,579 --> 00:05:04,579
The red high beam is the border peak of the merger.

56
00:05:04,579 --> 00:05:08,579
The blue high beam is the border peak of the non-merging merger.

57
00:05:08,579 --> 00:05:11,579
Click OK to exit.

58
00:05:11,579 --> 00:05:14,579
Thank you for watching. See you next time.

